course: dictionary
lesson: 12974
title: Exhausted: tired and used up
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Exhausted means extremely tired, with no energy left. You can often work it out from the clues around it. «After the football match, Sam was exhausted and flopped on the sofa.» The match and the flopping tell you he has used up all his energy.
explain: Exhausted can also mean completely used up, so none is left. «The farmer's well was exhausted, so there was no water for the sheep.» Try your meaning in the sentence: "there was no water left" fits, so you know you are right.
explain: Exhausted comes from the verb exhaust, which means to use up completely. Exhaust, exhausts, exhausted and exhausting are one family of words. «The long hike was exhausting.» Exhausting describes something that makes you tired, and exhausted describes the person who feels it.
fact: Exhausted is an adjective, and it is also the past form of the verb exhaust.
fact: «Exhausted» means extremely tired, with no energy left.
fact: «Exhausted» can also mean completely used up, so none is left.
fact: «Exhausting» means causing a lot of tiredness, as in «an exhausting day».
fact: Phrases to know: «completely exhausted» and «exhausted all the ideas».
exercise: «After the hard PE lesson, the runners were exhausted.» What does exhausted mean? | Lost in the park | Very excited and full of energy | * Extremely tired, with no energy left | Wet from the rain
exercise: «The town's coal supply was exhausted.» What does exhausted mean here? | Brand new and shiny | Hidden under the ground | * Completely used up, so none is left | Very tired and sleepy
exercise: Which word in «The climb was exhausting, but the view was worth it» means causing a lot of tiredness? | worth | view | * exhausting | climb
test: «Ben had run all day and felt exhausted.» What does exhausted mean? | * Extremely tired, with no energy left | Full of energy | Scared | Hungry
test: «The team had exhausted all their ideas.» What does exhausted mean here? | Found many new ideas | * Used up, so none are left | Shared with their friends | Written down on paper
exam: «After the long night shift, the nurse was exhausted.» What is the best meaning? | Lost in the hospital | Happy and wide awake | * Extremely tired, with no energy left | Cold and wet
